# core.autocrlf=true on this machine, so a file checked in from here gets CRLF in the working
# tree and, for a file created here, CRLF committed as well. That is harmless for Python and
# Markdown and fatal for a shell script: Linux reads the \r as part of the interpreter path and
# the script dies as `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` -- an error that names
# neither the script nor line endings, on a box rented by the hour.
#
# Added 2026-09-15 with serving/setup-vast.sh, the first file in this repo that has to run on
# something other than Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
